// spec: MOD-012
//
// CycA uses CycB and CycB uses CycA.  Both load, both bodies run, and the
// functions of each are callable -- because a module is loaded once by
// resolved path [MOD-003], so the second import finds the entry already made
// rather than descending again.
//
// ⚠️ This case exists because the specification said the opposite. MOD-012 read
// 'circular imports do not work', on the strength of a probe whose fixtures
// returned 'A' and 'B' from functions declared ': String'. A one-character
// literal is a Char [LEX-023], so those functions failed with 'Type mismatch!'
// whether or not a cycle existed.

uses 'modules/CycA';

WriteLn (AName ());
WriteLn (CycA.AName ());
